department-Administration = Facility administration
department-Administration-description = The Administrative Service oversees all areas of Foundation activity at every level. It includes all key communication nodes and command centers, each of which is duplicated. It is also responsible for managing all Foundation financial resources, including fund allocation, bookkeeping, budget planning, and so on. Due to its importance, staff working here are often subjected to loyalty checks. In addition to the core divisions, the Administrative Service has an internal unit responsible for all clerical paperwork and office administration, as well as archival duties.
department-MobileTaskForce = Mobile Task Forces
department-MobileTaskForce-description = Due to the nature of SCP Foundation operations, there is a need for many specialists with a fairly narrow focus. This usually applies to SCP objects that require substantial effort for successful containment, as well as nonstandard approaches. For these and other purposes, Mobile Task Forces are formed. Mobile Task Forces are small detachments (usually ten to thirty people, though groups with far larger numbers also exist), specializing in performing specific tasks or handling unusual situations. Each group is assigned a unique combination of a Greek letter and a number, though clarifying prefixes may also be used.
department-FondSecurity = Foundation security service
department-FondSecurity-description = "external police." This department of Security reports directly to regional command and is deployed to various Foundation facilities to carry out specific tasks. It is usually standard security personnel, but mobile.
department-EthicsCommittee = Ethics Committee
department-EthicsCommittee-description = The Ethics Committee determines what is ethical. Despite the Foundation’s utilitarian approach to moral dilemmas, the Ethics Committee ensures that only the necessary sacrifices are made and that the most ethical option is always chosen. Foundation personnel should remember that the Ethics Committee stands watch, evaluates, and renders judgment.
department-HeavyContainmentSecurityService = Special Forces Unit
department-HeavyContainmentSecurityService-description = Their duties include guarding objects and opposing them in situations where containment conditions are breached.
department-ExternalAdministrativeZoneSecurityService = Garrison Detachment
department-ExternalAdministrativeZoneSecurityService-description = "internal police." The detachment’s members are responsible for maintaining order among the staff of all Foundation facilities. Their duties also include protection of residential complexes, storage facilities not involved in SCP containment, and ensuring the secure detention of D-Class personnel.
department-ScientificService = Scientific Service
department-ScientificService-description = Effective work by the Scientific Service is the cornerstone of Foundation operations. The Scientific Service studies all contained and incoming SCP objects, develops countermeasures and neutralization procedures in the event of containment breaches, and develops various equipment, devices, compounds, and much more for the Foundation.
department-MedicalService = Medical Service
department-MedicalService-description = The Medical Service is responsible for keeping all Foundation personnel in good health. Due to the nature of the Foundation's work, medical staff regularly encounter the most difficult and often specialized cases of wounds, injuries, infections, and mental disorders, so only the best doctors are recruited into the Medical Service. Some Foundation physicians, after a certain period of work, gain one or another additional specialty directly related to dealing with a specific type of anomaly, such as memetic.
department-EngineeringTechnicalService = Engineering and Technical Service
department-EngineeringTechnicalService-description = The Engineering and Technical Service is responsible for technical and facility maintenance of any installations and equipment used by the Foundation. It is this service that designs and builds new Sites, Sectors, districts, other structures, and internal transport routes, as well as carries out all types of repair and upkeep. ITS staff are divided into several sections with different access levels and duties; staff with higher access levels therefore design and construct containment chambers for Keter-class objects and work with other strategic structures.
department-LogisticsService = Logistics Service
department-LogisticsService-description = The Logistics Service handles distribution of material, financial, and labor resources between Foundation facilities. Transportation is carried out using road, water, rail, air, space, and other forms of transport. There is a complex system for assigning priority and importance classes used when allocating particular resources; the highest priority is usually given to transported SCP objects of any class and resources required for their containment. Any obstacles arising during deliveries are removed first.
department-FoodAndSanitationServiceDepartment = Service Department
department-FoodAndSanitationServiceDepartment-description = The Service Department is an auxiliary subdivision of the SCP Foundation that ensures the operation of the staff's basic needs and maintains a comfortable living environment for personnel. This department is a structural grouping of three specialized groups: the Culinary Group, Floral Section, and Sanitation and Hygiene Sector.
department-LowAccessPersonnel = Class-D Personnel
department-LowAccessPersonnel-description = Class-D is assigned to expendable personnel used for work with extremely dangerous anomalies. Class-D personnel are usually recruited from prisons worldwide, with preference given to those convicted of violent crimes and especially those sentenced to death. Recruited personnel are transported to Foundation facilities under a credible pretext. Class-D personnel must be regularly subjected to mandatory psychiatric examinations, and by the end of the month either processed with Class-B amnestic (or stronger), or terminated, at the discretion of local Security or Medical Service. If a catastrophic event occurs at a facility, all local Class-D personnel are subject to immediate termination unless local Security decides otherwise.
department-SCP = SCP Objects
department-SCP-description = The living (and not-so-living) embodiment of the Foundation's nightmares. They are the reason scientists go gray, Security drinks antidepressants, and all of these protocols exist. They cannot be destroyed, they cannot be understood—only contained until they realize that the rules are not written by us.
